### Using a binding with a localization service

To switch the UI culture at runtime, you can change `CultureInfo.CurrentUICulture` and then restart the app to force the UI to reload with the new language. The following approach requires an app restart:

```csharp
var culture = new CultureInfo("es");
CultureInfo.CurrentUICulture = culture;
CultureInfo.CurrentCulture = culture;
AppResources.Culture = culture;
// App restart is required to refresh all UI elements
```

Because XAML bindings that use `x:Static` are evaluated only once at page load, a restart is the only reliable way to apply the new language without code‑behind hacks.

